                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Basic Information[/h1]\n[b]Title:[/b]  Spellbind\n[b]Developer:[/b]  Point2Point Entertainment\n[b]Publisher:[/b]  Strategy First \n[b]Genre:[/b]  Role-playing Game\n\n[h1]General Impression[/h1]\nI really wanted to give Spellbind a fair chance. I read the vast majority of negative reviews and still wanted to find some redeeming points to this game. Sadly, they were few and the only good aspect to this title, might be the generic yet decent enough 3D graphics and sound selection. That’s about it. Everything else from the AI, short gameplay and the downright game-breaking controls, make Spellbind feel highly unpolished even for an Early Access (which this game, is not) state. I received it in a well priced bundle but I can’t stress enough how much this RPG is overpriced for what it offers. If you can’t buy it at a sizeable discount, simply move on and seek far better alternatives. I can’t believe it doesn’t even offer Cards or Achivements to bolster its value to a marginal point at the very least…\n\n[h1]Strong Points[/h1]\n+ Decent  graphics and sounds.\n\n[h1]Weak Points[/h1]\n- Quite short and far too linear.\n- No Steam Trading Cards or Achievements.\n- Atrocious control scheme.\n- Highly overpriced.\n\n[b]Rating 4/10[/b]\n \n[quote]This review was submitted for [url=http://steamcommunity.com/groups/ImperialReviews]Imperial Reviews[/url] and [url=http://steamcommunity.com/groups/Xx_The_Kool_Kids_Klub_xX]Kool Kids Klub[/url].[/quote]",
